st it's tough for me to see that  knowing what I went through and I don't  want anyone else to have to go through  that so I decided to come out publicly  with what happened to me to hopefully  raise awareness more of my peers and say  you know I don't know how I got it and  it could really happen to anyone did you  think at one point you might not make it  Matt yeah when I was being wheeled down  the ICU I was definitely starting to  finally question myself it's up at that  point I was thinking you know I'm just  gonna get over it it's just a sickness  like I'm young I'm healthy  but being wheeled down to the ICU and  being in those remote Hall  where there's nobody I was with my  thoughts and I was thinking you know  this is kind of like this is scary now  and then while I was in ICU and all of  my symptoms just exploded and peeked and  how much care I was being given I was  finally thinking like you know I don't  know how this is gonna turn out I don't  know how this is gonna end up so that  was definitely a very scary moment for  me to think that Matt you're looking  great now you're talking to us what's  your prognosis how are you doing I'm  doing much better now I've had a lot of  time to recover at home now  I've just been basically sleeping away  the days and trying to get better as  much as I can but yeah definitely better  than it was
 

